---
import {
  PaletteMock,
  SandboxMock,
  ScriptsMock,
  HooksMock,
  ThemeMock,
  TagsMock,
  ShortcutsMock,
  ResumeMock,
  CliMock,
} from '../demo/ExtrasMocks';
---

<section class="details-section">
  <div class="details-inner">
    <h2 data-reveal>Power tools included</h2>
    <div class="details-grid bento">
      <div class="detail desk-wash desk-wash--graphite detail-span-4" data-reveal>
        <div class="desk-wash-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="desk-wash-field bento-lit-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="detail-title">Everything is three keystrokes away.</div>
        <p>
          ⌘K searches terminals, projects, tasks, and pull requests, ranked by how often you come back to
          them.
        </p>
        <div class="bento-stack" aria-hidden="true"><PaletteMock /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="detail desk-wash desk-wash--graphite detail-span-2" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        <div class="desk-wash-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="desk-wash-field bento-lit-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="detail-title">Untrusted code, contained.</div>
        <p>Agents run in a Lima VM that mounts only the task's worktree — or sandboxed in place with Seatbelt and Landlock, via nono.</p>
        <div class="bento-stack" aria-hidden="true"><SandboxMock /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="detail desk-wash desk-wash--graphite detail-span-2" data-reveal>
        <div class="desk-wash-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="desk-wash-field bento-lit-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="detail-title">The commands you always run.</div>
        <p>Dev server, tests, release — save them with the project and run them in any task's worktree.</p>
        <div class="bento-stack" aria-hidden="true"><ScriptsMock /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="detail desk-wash desk-wash--graphite detail-span-2" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        <div class="desk-wash-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="desk-wash-field bento-lit-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="detail-title">Hooks for every stage.</div>
        <p>Start, continue, run, review, done: each stage runs the command you give it, task context included.</p>
        <div class="bento-stack" aria-hidden="true"><HooksMock /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="detail desk-wash desk-wash--graphite detail-span-2" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
        <div class="desk-wash-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="desk-wash-field bento-lit-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="detail-title">Theme every token.</div>
        <p>Start from a preset or build your own — dark or light base, every color overridable, down to the ANSI palette.</p>
        <div class="bento-stack" aria-hidden="true"><ThemeMock /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="detail desk-wash desk-wash--graphite detail-span-2" data-reveal>
        <div class="desk-wash-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="desk-wash-field bento-lit-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="detail-title">Filter by tag.</div>
        <p>Tag terminals, then cut the stack to one tag — or group the home view by them.</p>
        <div class="bento-stack" aria-hidden="true"><TagsMock /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="detail desk-wash desk-wash--graphite detail-span-2" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        <div class="desk-wash-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="desk-wash-field bento-lit-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="detail-title">No pointer required.</div>
        <p>⌘1 through ⌘9 land on any terminal in the stack; the board, a new task, and a fresh terminal are each one chord away.</p>
        <div class="bento-stack" aria-hidden="true"><ShortcutsMock /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="detail desk-wash desk-wash--graphite detail-span-2" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
        <div class="desk-wash-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="desk-wash-field bento-lit-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="detail-title">Quit without losing the room.</div>
        <p>The next launch brings the session's terminals back in their worktrees, panels included.</p>
        <div class="bento-stack" aria-hidden="true"><ResumeMock /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="detail desk-wash desk-wash--graphite detail-span-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="desk-wash-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="desk-wash-field bento-lit-field" aria-hidden="true"><span class="desk-wash-grain"></span></div>
        <div class="detail-title">Your agent can drive all of it.</div>
        <p>
          The <code>ouijit</code> CLI lands in every terminal the app opens — sandboxed ones included, nothing
          to install. Tasks, tags, hooks, scripts, drafts, themes: everything on this page, as commands with
          JSON out.
        </p>
        <div class="bento-stack" aria-hidden="true"><CliMock /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
